DP  - 2003 Dec 1
TI  - Attomole peptide analysis by high-pressure matrix-assisted laser 
      desorption/ionization Fourier transform mass spectrometry.
PG  - 6449-54
AB  - A new high-pressure matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization (HP-MALDI) source 
      for FTMS has recently been described (O'Connor et al. J. Am. Soc. Mass Spectrom., 
      in press). Improvements to the source design, including the incorporation of a 
      new high-pressure gas channel plate, resulted in ions devoid of metastable 
      fragmentation and also in increased sensitivity compared to the HP-MALDI 
      prototype source design. The focus of this contribution is the evaluation of the 
      current HP-MALDI FTMS configuration. The use of nonconductive sample surfaces, 
      such as Parafilm and Teflon, was explored, and spectra from 30 amol of peptide 
      applied to these surfaces were routinely obtained. In addition, the current limit 
      of detection for this configuration is demonstrated to be 300 zmol for the 
      phosphopeptide RRREEE(pS)EEEAA using multishot accumulation of the ions from 15 
      laser shots in the hexapole and 1 scan. In addition, the performance of the new 
      HP-MALDI FTMS configuration and its potential application for high-throughput 
      proteomics analyses are discussed.
